IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `ei1-payment`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Part I, "Benefit Period": ss 9, 10 and 11. Layer 1 of piece ei1.
-- Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30.
-- This module imports ei1-payment.l4 because s 10(13) to (15) read the maximum weeks of s 12(3).
-- A week is identified by the DATE of its Sunday (the core); a benefit period begins on a Sunday (s 10(1)).

§ `Section 9 - establishing a benefit period`

-- src:236 | 9 When an insured person who qualifies under section 7 or 7.1 makes an initial claim for benefits, a benefit period shall be established and, once it is established, benefits are payable to the person in accordance with this Part for each week of unemployment that falls in the benefit period.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 9 (src:236)
GIVEN `the insured person qualifies under section 7 or 7.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insured person makes an initial claim for benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 9 a benefit period shall be established` IF
        `the insured person qualifies under section 7 or 7.1`
    AND `the insured person makes an initial claim for benefits`

@ref Employment Insurance Act s 9 (src:236)
GIVEN `a benefit period has been established` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the week is a week of unemployment that falls in the benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 9 benefits are payable to the person in accordance with Part I for the week` IF
        `a benefit period has been established`
    AND `the week is a week of unemployment that falls in the benefit period`

§ `Section 10(1) to (3) - beginning, length and overlap`

-- src:238 | 10 (1) A benefit period begins on the later of
-- src:239 | (a) the Sunday of the week in which the interruption of earnings occurs, and
-- src:240 | (b) the Sunday of the week in which the initial claim for benefits is made.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 10(1) (src:238-240)
GIVEN -- out of range: reg 14 and reg 14.01 (piece er1) say when an interruption of earnings occurs
      `the day on which the interruption of earnings occurs` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the initial claim for benefits is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 10(1) the first day of the benefit period` IS
    IF `the Sunday of the week in which the interruption of earnings occurs` AT LEAST `the Sunday of the week in which the initial claim for benefits is made`
    THEN `the Sunday of the week in which the interruption of earnings occurs`
    ELSE `the Sunday of the week in which the initial claim for benefits is made`
    WHERE
        `the Sunday of the week in which the interruption of earnings occurs` MEANS
            `s 2(1) the Sunday that begins the week containing` `the day on which the interruption of earnings occurs`
        `the Sunday of the week in which the initial claim for benefits is made` MEANS
            `s 2(1) the Sunday that begins the week containing` `the day on which the initial claim for benefits is made`

-- src:242 | (2) Except as otherwise provided in subsections (10) to (15) and section 24, the length of a benefit period is 52 weeks.
-- "Except as otherwise provided in subsections (10) to (15) and section 24": the extensions are s 10(10) to (15) below;
-- section 24 (piece ei2) lets regulations extend a benefit period for work-sharing weeks (paragraph 24(1)(g)).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 10(2) (src:242)
`s 10(2) the length of a benefit period in weeks, before any extension` MEANS 52

-- src:244 | (3) Subject to a change or cancellation of a benefit period under this section, a benefit period shall not be established for the claimant if a prior benefit period has not ended.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 10(3) (src:244)
GIVEN `a prior benefit period has not ended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 10(3) a benefit period shall not be established for the claimant` IF
    `a prior benefit period has not ended`

@ref Employment Insurance Act s 9, s 10(3) (src:236) (src:244)
GIVEN `a benefit period shall be established under section 9` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a benefit period shall not be established because a prior benefit period has not ended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 9 and s 10(3) a benefit period is established for the claimant` IF
        `a benefit period shall be established under section 9`
    AND NOT (`a benefit period shall not be established because a prior benefit period has not ended`)

§ `Section 10(4) to (5.3) - late claims`

-- src:246 | (4) An initial claim for benefits made after the day when the claimant was first qualified to make the claim shall be regarded as having been made on an earlier day if the claimant shows that the claimant qualified to receive benefits on the earlier day and that there was good cause for the delay throughout the period beginning on the earlier day and ending on the day when the initial claim was made.
-- "Made after the day when the claimant was first qualified to make the claim"; the claimant must show that they
-- qualified on the earlier day and that there was good cause for the delay throughout the period from the earlier day
-- to the day the claim was made. The earlier day is the one the claimant asks for.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 10(4) (src:246)
GIVEN `the day on which the initial claim for benefits was made` IS A DATE
      `the day when the claimant was first qualified to make the claim` IS A DATE
      `the earlier day` IS A DATE
      `the claimant shows that the claimant qualified to receive benefits on the earlier day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant shows that there was good cause for the delay throughout the period beginning on the earlier day and ending on the day when the initial claim was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 10(4) the initial claim for benefits is regarded as having been made on the earlier day` IF
        `the day on which the initial claim for benefits was made` ABOVE `the day when the claimant was first qualified to make the claim`
    AND `the earlier day` BELOW `the day on which the initial claim for benefits was made`
    AND `the claimant shows that the claimant qualified to receive benefits on the earlier day`
    AND `the claimant shows that there was good cause for the delay throughout the period beginning on the earlier day and ending on the day when the initial claim was made`

-- src:248 | (5) A claim for benefits, other than an initial claim for benefits, made after the time prescribed for making the claim shall be regarded as having been made on an earlier day if the claimant shows that there was good cause for the delay throughout the period beginning on the earlier day and ending on the day when the claim was made.
-- The time prescribed for making the claim is the Regulations' (reg 26, piece er2); the last day of that time is an input.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 10(5) (src:248)
GIVEN `the day on which the claim for benefits was made` IS A DATE
      -- out of range: reg 26 (piece er2)
      `the last day of the time prescribed for making the claim` IS A DATE
      `the earlier day` IS A DATE
      `the claimant shows that there was good cause for the delay throughout the period beginning on the earlier day and ending on the day when the claim was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 10(5) the claim for benefits other than an initial claim is regarded as having been made on the earlier day` IF
        `the day on which the claim for benefits was made` ABOVE `the last day of the time prescribed for making the claim`
    AND `the earlier day` BELOW `the day on which the claim for benefits was made`
    AND `the claimant shows that there was good cause for the delay throughout the period beginning on the earlier day and ending on the day when the claim was made`

-- src:250 | (5.1) A claim for benefits referred to in section 23.1 with respect to a family member shall not be regarded as having been made on an earlier day under subsection (4) or (5) if
-- src:251 | (a) at the time the claim is made, all benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to that claim have already been exhausted;
-- src:252 | (b) the beginning of the period referred to in subsection 23.1(4) has already been determined with respect to that family member and the claim would have the effect of moving the beginning of that period to an earlier date; or
-- src:253 | (c) the claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations.
-- Paragraph (c) refers to circumstances "set out in the regulations". The Regulations deposited (current to
-- 2026-09-30) name none for this subsection, so it is an input.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 10(5.1) (src:250-253)
GIVEN `the claim would be regarded as having been made on an earlier day under subsection (4) or (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time the claim is made, all benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to that claim have already been exhausted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the beginning of the period referred to in subsection 23.1(4) has already been determined with respect to that family member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim would have the effect of moving the beginning of that period to an earlier date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 10(5.1) a claim for benefits referred to in section 23.1 is regarded as having been made on an earlier day` IF
        `the claim would be regarded as having been made on an earlier day under subsection (4) or (5)`
    AND NOT (   `at the time the claim is made, all benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to that claim have already been exhausted`
             OR (`the beginning of the period referred to in subsection 23.1(4) has already been determined with respect to that family member` AND `the claim would have the effect of moving the beginning of that period to an earlier date`)
             OR `the claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations`)

-- src:255 | (5.2) A claim for benefits referred to in section 23.2 with respect to a critically ill child must not be regarded as having been made on an earlier day under subsection (4) or (5) if
-- src:256 | (a) at the time the claim is made, all benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to that claim have already been exhausted;
-- src:257 | (b) the beginning of the period referred to in subsection 23.2(3) has already been determined with respect to that child and the claim would have the effect of moving the beginning of that period to an earlier date; or
-- src:258 | (c) the claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 10(5.2) (src:255-258)
GIVEN `the claim would be regarded as having been made on an earlier day under subsection (4) or (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time the claim is made, all benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to that claim have already been exhausted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the beginning of the period referred to in subsection 23.2(3) has already been determined with respect to that child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim would have the effect of moving the beginning of that period to an earlier date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 10(5.2) a claim for benefits referred to in section 23.2 is regarded as having been made on an earlier day` IF
        `the claim would be regarded as having been made on an earlier day under subsection (4) or (5)`
    AND NOT (   `at the time the claim is made, all benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to that claim have already been exhausted`
             OR (`the beginning of the period referred to in subsection 23.2(3) has already been determined with respect to that child` AND `the claim would have the effect of moving the beginning of that period to an earlier date`)
             OR `the claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations`)

-- src:260 | (5.3) A claim for benefits referred to in section 23.3 with respect to a critically ill adult must not be regarded as having been made on an earlier day under subsection (4) or (5) if
-- src:261 | (a) at the time the claim is made, all benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to that claim have already been exhausted;
-- src:262 | (b) the beginning of the period referred to in subsection 23.3(3) has already been determined with respect to that adult and the claim would have the effect of moving the beginning of that period to an earlier date; or
-- src:263 | (c) the claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 10(5.3) (src:260-263)
GIVEN `the claim would be regarded as having been made on an earlier day under subsection (4) or (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time the claim is made, all benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to that claim have already been exhausted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the beginning of the period referred to in subsection 23.3(3) has already been determined with respect to that adult` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim would have the effect of moving the beginning of that period to an earlier date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 10(5.3) a claim for benefits referred to in section 23.3 is regarded as having been made on an earlier day` IF
        `the claim would be regarded as having been made on an earlier day under subsection (4) or (5)`
    AND NOT (   `at the time the claim is made, all benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to that claim have already been exhausted`
             OR (`the beginning of the period referred to in subsection 23.3(3) has already been determined with respect to that adult` AND `the claim would have the effect of moving the beginning of that period to an earlier date`)
             OR `the claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations`)

§ `Section 10(6) to (9) - cancelling and ending a benefit period`

-- src:265 | (6) Once a benefit period has been established for a claimant, the Commission may
-- src:266 | (a) cancel the benefit period if it has ended and no benefits were paid or payable during the period; or
-- The Commission "may" cancel: the rule says whether the power is open to it (its conditions are met), not whether it
-- will use it.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 10(6)(a) (src:265-266)
GIVEN `the benefit period has ended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no benefits were paid or payable during the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 10(6)(a) the Commission may cancel the benefit period` IF
        `the benefit period has ended`
    AND `no benefits were paid or payable during the period`

-- src:267 | (b) whether or not the period has ended, cancel at the request of the claimant that portion of the benefit period immediately before the first week for which benefits were paid or payable, if the claimant
-- src:268 | (i) establishes under this Part, as an insured person, a new benefit period beginning the first week for which benefits were paid or payable or establishes, under Part VII.1, as a self-employed person within the meaning of subsection 152.01(1), a new benefit period beginning the first week for which benefits were paid or payable, and
-- src:269 | (ii) shows that there was good cause for the delay in making the request throughout the period beginning on the day when benefits were first paid or payable and ending on the day when the request for cancellation was made.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 10(6)(b) (src:267-269)
GIVEN `the claimant asks for the cancellation of that portion of the benefit period immediately before the first week for which benefits were paid or payable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant establishes under this Part, as an insured person, a new benefit period beginning the first week for which benefits were paid or payable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant establishes under Part VII.1, as a self-employed person within the meaning of subsection 152.01(1), a new benefit period beginning the first week for which benefits were paid or payable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant shows that there was good cause for the delay in making the request throughout the period beginning on the day when benefits were first paid or payable and ending on the day when the request for cancellation was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 10(6)(b) the Commission may cancel at the request of the claimant the portion of the benefit period immediately before the first week for which benefits were paid or payable` IF
        `the claimant asks for the cancellation of that portion of the benefit period immediately before the first week for which benefits were paid or payable`
    AND (   `the claimant establishes under this Part, as an insured person, a new benefit period beginning the first week for which benefits were paid or payable`
         OR `the claimant establishes under Part VII.1, as a self-employed person within the meaning of subsection 152.01(1), a new benefit period beginning the first week for which benefits were paid or payable`)
    AND `the claimant shows that there was good cause for the delay in making the request throughout the period beginning on the day when benefits were first paid or payable and ending on the day when the request for cancellation was made`

-- src:271 | (7) A cancelled benefit period or portion of a benefit period is deemed never to have begun.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 10(7) (src:271)
GIVEN `the benefit period or portion of a benefit period has been cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 10(7) the cancelled benefit period or portion of a benefit period is deemed never to have begun` IF
    `the benefit period or portion of a benefit period has been cancelled`

-- Helper: a date that may be absent, as a list of at most one date.
GIVEN day IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
DECIDE `ei1 the dates in` IS
    CONSIDER day
    WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
    WHEN JUST d THEN LIST d

-- src:277 | (d) the claimant
-- src:278 | (i) requests that their benefit period end,
-- src:279 | (ii) makes a new initial claim for benefits under this Part or Part VII.1, and
-- src:280 | (iii) qualifies, as an insured person, to receive benefits under this Part or qualifies, as a self-employed person within the meaning of subsection 152.01(1), to receive benefits under Part VII.1.
-- Paragraph (d) happens when the last of its three things has happened: the request, the new initial claim and the
-- claimant's qualifying under this Part (as an insured person) or Part VII.1 (as a self-employed person).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 10(8)(d) (src:277-280)
GIVEN `the day on which the claimant requests that their benefit period end` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the claimant makes a new initial claim for benefits under this Part or Part VII.1` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the claimant qualifies, as an insured person, to receive benefits under this Part or qualifies, as a self-employed person within the meaning of subsection 152.01(1), to receive benefits under Part VII.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `s 10(8)(d) the day on which the claimant requests the end of the benefit period, makes a new initial claim and qualifies` IS
    IF NOT (`the claimant qualifies, as an insured person, to receive benefits under this Part or qualifies, as a self-employed person within the meaning of subsection 152.01(1), to receive benefits under Part VII.1`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the day on which the claimant requests that their benefit period end`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST requested THEN
             CONSIDER `the day on which the claimant makes a new initial claim for benefits under this Part or Part VII.1`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
             WHEN JUST claimed THEN JUST (IF requested AT LEAST claimed THEN requested ELSE claimed)

-- src:273 | (8) A benefit period ends when any of the following first occurs:
-- src:274 | (a) no further benefits are payable to the claimant in their benefit period, including for the reason that benefits have been paid for the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid under section 12;
-- src:275 | (b) the benefit period would otherwise end under this section; or
-- src:276 | (c) [Repealed, 2002, c. 9, s. 12]
-- "When any of the following first occurs": the earliest of the days on which (a), (b) or (d) happens.
-- Paragraph (c) is repealed (src line 276).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 10(8) (src:273-276)
GIVEN `the day on which no further benefits are payable to the claimant in their benefit period, including because benefits have been paid for the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid under section 12` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the benefit period would otherwise end under this section` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the claimant requests the end of the benefit period, makes a new initial claim and qualifies` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 10(8) the day on which the benefit period ends` IS
    Date (minimum (map (GIVEN x YIELD Day x)
                       (append (append (`ei1 the dates in` `the day on which no further benefits are payable to the claimant in their benefit period, including because benefits have been paid for the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid under section 12`)
                                       (LIST `the day on which the benefit period would otherwise end under this section`))
                               (`ei1 the dates in` `the day on which the claimant requests the end of the benefit period, makes a new initial claim and qualifies`))))

-- src:282 | (9) Whether or not the benefit period has ended, a request under paragraph 8(d) shall be regarded as having been made on an earlier day if the claimant shows that there was good cause for the delay throughout the period beginning on the earlier day and ending on the day when the request was made.
-- The text says "a request under paragraph 8(d)": read as paragraph 10(8)(d) (fork F-9 in NOTES.md).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 10(9) (src:282)
GIVEN `the day on which the request was made` IS A DATE
      `the earlier day` IS A DATE
      `the claimant shows that there was good cause for the delay throughout the period beginning on the earlier day and ending on the day when the request was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 10(9) the request under paragraph 10(8)(d) is regarded as having been made on the earlier day` IF
        `the earlier day` BELOW `the day on which the request was made`
    AND `the claimant shows that there was good cause for the delay throughout the period beginning on the earlier day and ending on the day when the request was made`

§ `Section 10(10) to (12.1) - extensions of the benefit period`

-- src:284 | (10) A claimant’s benefit period is extended by the aggregate of any weeks during the benefit period for which the claimant proves, in such manner as the Commission may direct, that the claimant was not entitled to benefits because the claimant was
-- src:285 | (a) confined in a jail, penitentiary or other similar institution and was not found guilty of the offence for which the claimant was being held or any other offence arising out of the same transaction;
-- src:286 | (b) in receipt of earnings paid because of the complete severance of their relationship with their former employer;
-- src:287 | (c) in receipt of workers’ compensation payments for an illness or injury; or
-- src:288 | (d) in receipt of payments under a provincial law on the basis of having ceased to work because continuing to work would have resulted in danger to the claimant, her unborn child or a child whom she was breast-feeding.
-- The claimant must prove the reason "in such manner as the Commission may direct": the first input is that proof,
-- taken as given. Paragraph (a) needs a person held but not found guilty, so being found guilty is its own input.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 10(10) (src:284-288)
GIVEN `the claimant proves, in the manner the Commission directs, that the claimant was not entitled to benefits in the week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant was confined in a jail, penitentiary or other similar institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant was found guilty of the offence for which the claimant was being held or any other offence arising out of the same transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant was in receipt of earnings paid because of the complete severance of their relationship with their former employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant was in receipt of workers' compensation payments for an illness or injury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant was in receipt of payments under a provincial law on the basis of having ceased to work because continuing to work would have resulted in danger to the claimant, her unborn child or a child whom she was breast-feeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 10(10) the week is one for which the claimant was not entitled to benefits for a reason that extends the benefit period` IF
        `the claimant proves, in the manner the Commission directs, that the claimant was not entitled to benefits in the week`
    AND (   (`the claimant was confined in a jail, penitentiary or other similar institution` AND NOT (`the claimant was found guilty of the offence for which the claimant was being held or any other offence arising out of the same transaction`))
         OR `the claimant was in receipt of earnings paid because of the complete severance of their relationship with their former employer`
         OR `the claimant was in receipt of workers' compensation payments for an illness or injury`
         OR `the claimant was in receipt of payments under a provincial law on the basis of having ceased to work because continuing to work would have resulted in danger to the claimant, her unborn child or a child whom she was breast-feeding`)

-- src:290 | (11) A claimant’s benefit period is extended by the aggregate of any weeks during an extension of a benefit period under subsection (10) for which the claimant proves, in such manner as the Commission may direct, that the claimant was not entitled to benefits because of a reason specified in that subsection.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 10(11) (src:290)
GIVEN `the week falls during an extension of the benefit period under subsection (10)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the week is one for which the claimant was not entitled to benefits for a reason that extends the benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 10(11) the week during an extension further extends the benefit period` IF
        `the week falls during an extension of the benefit period under subsection (10)`
    AND `the week is one for which the claimant was not entitled to benefits for a reason that extends the benefit period`

-- src:284 | (10) A claimant’s benefit period is extended by the aggregate of any weeks during the benefit period for which the claimant proves, in such manner as the Commission may direct, that the claimant was not entitled to benefits because the claimant was
-- src:285 | (a) confined in a jail, penitentiary or other similar institution and was not found guilty of the offence for which the claimant was being held or any other offence arising out of the same transaction;
-- src:286 | (b) in receipt of earnings paid because of the complete severance of their relationship with their former employer;
-- src:287 | (c) in receipt of workers’ compensation payments for an illness or injury; or
-- src:288 | (d) in receipt of payments under a provincial law on the basis of having ceased to work because continuing to work would have resulted in danger to the claimant, her unborn child or a child whom she was breast-feeding.
-- src:289 | Further extension of benefit period
-- src:290 | (11) A claimant’s benefit period is extended by the aggregate of any weeks during an extension of a benefit period under subsection (10) for which the claimant proves, in such manner as the Commission may direct, that the claimant was not entitled to benefits because of a reason specified in that subsection.
-- The weeks are counted once each: the first count is of weeks during the benefit period (subsection (10)), the second
-- of weeks during that extension (subsection (11)).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 10(10), s 10(11) (src:284) (src:290)
GIVEN `the number of weeks during the benefit period for which the claimant proves that the claimant was not entitled to benefits for a reason specified in subsection (10)` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of weeks during an extension under subsection (10) for which the claimant proves that the claimant was not entitled to benefits for a reason specified in that subsection` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 10(10) and s 10(11) the number of weeks by which the benefit period is extended` IS
    `the number of weeks during the benefit period for which the claimant proves that the claimant was not entitled to benefits for a reason specified in subsection (10)`
    PLUS `the number of weeks during an extension under subsection (10) for which the claimant proves that the claimant was not entitled to benefits for a reason specified in that subsection`

-- src:292 | (12) If the child or children referred to in subsection 23(1) are hospitalized during the period referred to in subsection 23(2), the benefit period is extended by the number of weeks during which the child or children are hospitalized.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 10(12) (src:292)
GIVEN `the child or children referred to in subsection 23(1) are hospitalized during the period referred to in subsection 23(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of weeks during which the child or children are hospitalized` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 10(12) the number of weeks by which the benefit period is extended because the children are in hospital` IS
    IF `the child or children referred to in subsection 23(1) are hospitalized during the period referred to in subsection 23(2)`
    THEN `the number of weeks during which the child or children are hospitalized`
    ELSE 0

-- src:294 | (12.1) If, during the period referred to in subsection 23(2), the start date of a claimant’s period of parental leave is deferred or a claimant is directed to return to duty from parental leave, in accordance with regulations made under the National Defence Act, the benefit period is extended by the number of weeks during which the claimant’s parental leave is deferred or the claimant is directed to return to duty, as the case may be.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 10(12.1) (src:294)
GIVEN `during the period referred to in subsection 23(2), the start date of the claimant's period of parental leave is deferred or the claimant is directed to return to duty from parental leave, in accordance with regulations made under the National Defence Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of weeks during which the claimant's parental leave is deferred or the claimant is directed to return to duty` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 10(12.1) the number of weeks by which the benefit period is extended because of the Canadian Forces` IS
    IF `during the period referred to in subsection 23(2), the start date of the claimant's period of parental leave is deferred or the claimant is directed to return to duty from parental leave, in accordance with regulations made under the National Defence Act`
    THEN `the number of weeks during which the claimant's parental leave is deferred or the claimant is directed to return to duty`
    ELSE 0

§ `Section 10(13) to (15) - extensions for special benefits`

-- The benefits paid for one of the reasons in paragraphs 12(3)(a) to (f) during the benefit period: the reason and the
-- number of weeks for which benefits were paid for it.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 10(13) (src:296-299)
DECLARE `ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason` HAS
    `ei1 the reason for which special benefits were paid`                  IS A `Reason for benefits`
    `ei1 the number of weeks for which special benefits were paid for it`  IS A NUMBER

-- Only reasons in paragraphs 12(3)(a) to (f) for which benefits were in fact paid (at least one week) are "reasons for
-- which benefits were paid" in the sense of s 10(13). An entry for the regular reason (a reason other than those mentioned
-- in subsection 12(3)) is not one of them and is dropped, so the list may be passed whole.
GIVEN paid IS A LIST OF `ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason`
GIVETH A LIST OF `ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason`
DECIDE `ei1 the special benefits actually paid` IS
    filter (GIVEN p YIELD     p's `ei1 the number of weeks for which special benefits were paid for it` GREATER THAN 0
                          AND NOT (p's `ei1 the reason for which special benefits were paid` EQUALS `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)`))
           paid

-- src:298 | (b) benefits were paid to the claimant for more than one of the reasons mentioned in paragraphs 12(3)(a) to (f) and at least one of those benefits was paid for fewer than the applicable maximum number of weeks established for those reasons, and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 10(13) (src:298)
GIVEN paid IS A `ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason`
      election IS AN `Election of maximum weeks`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 10(13) the maximum number of weeks established for the reason for which special benefits were paid` IS
    fromMaybe 0 (`s 12(3) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in a benefit period for the reason` (paid's `ei1 the reason for which special benefits were paid`) election)

-- src:299 | (c) the maximum total number of weeks established for those reasons is greater than 50,
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 10(13) (src:299)
GIVEN paid IS A LIST OF `ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason`
      election IS AN `Election of maximum weeks`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 10(13)(c) the maximum total number of weeks established for the reasons for which special benefits were paid` IS
    sum (map (GIVEN p YIELD `s 10(13) the maximum number of weeks established for the reason for which special benefits were paid` p election) (`ei1 the special benefits actually paid` paid))

-- src:296 | (13) If, during a claimant’s benefit period,
-- src:297 | (a) regular benefits were not paid to the claimant,
-- src:298 | (b) benefits were paid to the claimant for more than one of the reasons mentioned in paragraphs 12(3)(a) to (f) and at least one of those benefits was paid for fewer than the applicable maximum number of weeks established for those reasons, and
-- src:299 | (c) the maximum total number of weeks established for those reasons is greater than 50,
-- src:300 | the benefit period is extended so that those benefits may be paid up to that maximum total number of weeks.
-- (a) regular benefits were not paid; (b) benefits were paid for more than one of the reasons in paragraphs 12(3)(a)
-- to (f) and at least one of those benefits was paid for fewer than the applicable maximum; (c) the maximum total
-- number of weeks established for those reasons is greater than 50.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 10(13) (src:296-300)
GIVEN `regular benefits were paid to the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      paid IS A LIST OF `ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason`
      election IS AN `Election of maximum weeks`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 10(13) the benefit period is extended so that special benefits may be paid up to the maximum total number of weeks` IF
        NOT (`regular benefits were paid to the claimant`)
    AND count (`ei1 the special benefits actually paid` paid) AT LEAST 2
    AND any (GIVEN p YIELD p's `ei1 the number of weeks for which special benefits were paid for it` BELOW `s 10(13) the maximum number of weeks established for the reason for which special benefits were paid` p election) (`ei1 the special benefits actually paid` paid)
    AND `s 10(13)(c) the maximum total number of weeks established for the reasons for which special benefits were paid` paid election GREATER THAN 50

-- src:315 | (15) Subject to subsection (14), unless the benefit period is also extended under any of subsections (10) to (12.1), an extension under subsection (13) must not result in a benefit period of more than the sum of two weeks and the total of the maximum number of weeks established under subsection 12(3) for each of the benefits paid to the claimant for one of the reasons mentioned in paragraphs 12(3)(a) to (f) during the claimant’s benefit period before it was extended under subsection (13).
-- Two weeks more than the total of the maxima of the benefits paid (the waiting week and the week for which the claim
-- is made), but never more than the 104 weeks of subsection (14). The opening words of s 10(15), "unless the benefit period is
-- also extended under any of subsections (10) to (12.1)", lift this limit for a claimant who has one of those extensions; that
-- exemption is NOT modelled (fork F-13 in NOTES.md): the same target length is used and only s 10(14) limits the total. This is the length that subsection (13) extends the
-- benefit period to, and the figure that s 12(5) takes (as the maximum weeks "calculated under subsection 10(15)").
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 10(15), s 10(14) (src:315) (src:312)
GIVEN paid IS A LIST OF `ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason`
      election IS AN `Election of maximum weeks`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 10(15) the maximum number of weeks in a benefit period extended under subsection (13)` IS
    min 104 (2 PLUS `s 10(13)(c) the maximum total number of weeks established for the reasons for which special benefits were paid` paid election)

-- src:296 | (13) If, during a claimant’s benefit period,
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 10(13), s 10(15) (src:296) (src:315)
GIVEN `regular benefits were paid to the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      paid IS A LIST OF `ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason`
      election IS AN `Election of maximum weeks`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 10(13) the number of weeks by which the benefit period is extended` IS
    IF `s 10(13) the benefit period is extended so that special benefits may be paid up to the maximum total number of weeks` `regular benefits were paid to the claimant` paid election
    THEN max 0 (`s 10(15) the maximum number of weeks in a benefit period extended under subsection (13)` paid election MINUS `s 10(2) the length of a benefit period in weeks, before any extension`)
    ELSE 0

-- src:302 | (13.01) The benefit period is extended by 26 weeks so that benefits may be paid for the reason mentioned in paragraph 12(3)(b) up to the maximum number of weeks if, during a claimant’s benefit period,
-- src:303 | (a) benefits were paid to the claimant for that reason and the applicable maximum number of weeks is established in subparagraph 12(3)(b)(ii);
-- src:304 | (b) regular benefits were not paid to the claimant; and
-- src:305 | (c) benefits were not paid for any reason mentioned in paragraph 12(3)(a), (c), (d), (e) or (f).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 10(13.01) (src:302-305)
GIVEN `benefits were paid to the claimant for the reason mentioned in paragraph 12(3)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      election IS AN `Election of maximum weeks`
      `regular benefits were paid to the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `benefits were paid for any reason mentioned in paragraph 12(3)(a), (c), (d), (e) or (f)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 10(13.01) the number of weeks by which the benefit period is extended for the reason mentioned in paragraph 12(3)(b)` IS
    IF     `benefits were paid to the claimant for the reason mentioned in paragraph 12(3)(b)`
       AND election EQUALS `the 61-week maximum`
       AND NOT (`regular benefits were paid to the claimant`)
       AND NOT (`benefits were paid for any reason mentioned in paragraph 12(3)(a), (c), (d), (e) or (f)`)
    THEN 26
    ELSE 0

-- src:307 | (13.02) If, during a claimant’s benefit period, regular benefits were paid, benefits were paid for the reason mentioned in paragraph 12(3)(b) in the case where the applicable maximum number of weeks is established under subparagraph 12(3)(b)(ii), and benefits were paid for fewer than the total number of weeks established under subsection 12(6) as determined under subsection 12(7), the benefit period is extended so that benefits may be paid up to that total number of weeks. The extension must not exceed 26 weeks.
-- "Benefits were paid for fewer than the total number of weeks established under subsection 12(6) as determined under
-- subsection 12(7)": the shortfall, in weeks of the benefit period, that the extension has to cover is not worked out
-- by the text (it turns on the Schedule IV conversion of s 12(7)), so it is an input; the extension never exceeds 26.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 10(13.02) (src:307)
GIVEN `regular benefits were paid to the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `benefits were paid for the reason mentioned in paragraph 12(3)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      election IS AN `Election of maximum weeks`
      `benefits were paid for fewer than the total number of weeks established under subsection 12(6) as determined under subsection 12(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of weeks by which the benefit period must be extended so that benefits may be paid up to that total number of weeks` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 10(13.02) the number of weeks by which the benefit period is extended for regular and special benefits` IS
    IF     `regular benefits were paid to the claimant`
       AND `benefits were paid for the reason mentioned in paragraph 12(3)(b)`
       AND election EQUALS `the 61-week maximum`
       AND `benefits were paid for fewer than the total number of weeks established under subsection 12(6) as determined under subsection 12(7)`
    THEN min 26 (max 0 `the number of weeks by which the benefit period must be extended so that benefits may be paid up to that total number of weeks`)
    ELSE 0

-- src:309 | (13.03) Only the regular benefits and benefits for any of the reasons mentioned in paragraphs 12(3)(a) to (f) that were paid during the claimant’s benefit period before it was extended under subsection (13.02) are payable during that extension.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 10(13.03) (src:309)
GIVEN `benefits of that kind were paid during the claimant's benefit period before it was extended under subsection (13.02)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 10(13.03) benefits of that kind are payable during the extension under subsection (13.02)` IF
    `benefits of that kind were paid during the claimant's benefit period before it was extended under subsection (13.02)`

-- s 10(13.1) to (13.7): [Repealed, 2016, c. 7, s. 211] (src lines 310-311). Nothing to encode.

-- src:312 | (14) An extension under one or more of subsections (10) to (13.02) must not result in a benefit period of more than 104 weeks.
-- The 104 weeks bind extensions under (10) to (13.02). An extension under section 24 (piece ei2), which a regulation
-- may add for work-sharing weeks, is not one of those and is added afterwards.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 10(14) (src:312)
`s 10(14) the longest benefit period after extensions under subsections (10) to (13.02), in weeks` MEANS 104

@ref Employment Insurance Act s 10(2), s 10(10) to (15) (src:242) (src:284) (src:312)
GIVEN -- the extensions of subsections (10) to (11), (12), (12.1), (13), (13.01) and (13.02), in weeks
      `the weeks of extension under subsections (10) and (11)` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks of extension under subsection (12)` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks of extension under subsection (12.1)` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks of extension under subsection (13)` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks of extension under subsection (13.01)` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks of extension under subsection (13.02)` IS A NUMBER
      -- out of range: section 24(1)(g) and the regulations made under it (pieces ei2, er3)
      `the weeks of extension under regulations made under paragraph 24(1)(g)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 10(2) and s 10(14) the length of the benefit period in weeks` IS
    min `s 10(14) the longest benefit period after extensions under subsections (10) to (13.02), in weeks`
        (`s 10(2) the length of a benefit period in weeks, before any extension`
         PLUS `the weeks of extension under subsections (10) and (11)`
         PLUS `the weeks of extension under subsection (12)`
         PLUS `the weeks of extension under subsection (12.1)`
         PLUS `the weeks of extension under subsection (13)`
         PLUS `the weeks of extension under subsection (13.01)`
         PLUS `the weeks of extension under subsection (13.02)`)
    PLUS `the weeks of extension under regulations made under paragraph 24(1)(g)`

-- s 10(14.1): [Repealed, 2016, c. 7, s. 211] (src line 313). Nothing to encode.

§ `Section 11 - a week of unemployment`

-- src:317 | 11 (1) A week of unemployment for a claimant is a week in which the claimant does not work a full working week.
-- "Full working week" is the Regulations' (regs 29 to 31, piece er2); whether the claimant works one is an input.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 11(1) (src:317)
GIVEN -- out of range: regs 29 to 31 (piece er2)
      `the claimant works a full working week` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 11(1) the week is a week in which the claimant does not work a full working week` IF
    NOT (`the claimant works a full working week`)

-- src:319 | (2) A week during which a claimant’s contract of service continues and in respect of which the claimant receives or will receive their usual remuneration for a full working week is not a week of unemployment, even though the claimant may be excused from performing their normal duties or does not have any duties to perform at that time.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 11(2) (src:319)
GIVEN `the claimant's contract of service continues during the week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant receives or will receive their usual remuneration for a full working week in respect of the week` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 11(2) the week is not a week of unemployment although the claimant is excused from their normal duties` IF
        `the claimant's contract of service continues during the week`
    AND `the claimant receives or will receive their usual remuneration for a full working week in respect of the week`

-- src:321 | (3) A week or part of a week during a period of leave from employment is not a week of unemployment if the employee
-- src:322 | (a) takes the period of leave under an agreement with their employer;
-- src:323 | (b) continues to be an employee of the employer during the period; and
-- src:324 | (c) receives remuneration that was set aside during a period of work, regardless of when it is paid.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 11(3) (src:321-324)
GIVEN `the week or part of a week is during a period of leave from employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee takes the period of leave under an agreement with their employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee continues to be an employee of the employer during the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee receives remuneration that was set aside during a period of work, regardless of when it is paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 11(3) the week or part of a week during a period of leave is not a week of unemployment` IF
        `the week or part of a week is during a period of leave from employment`
    AND `the employee takes the period of leave under an agreement with their employer`
    AND `the employee continues to be an employee of the employer during the period`
    AND `the employee receives remuneration that was set aside during a period of work, regardless of when it is paid`

-- src:326 | (4) An insured person is deemed to have worked a full working week during each week that falls wholly or partly in a period of leave if
-- src:327 | (a) in each week the insured person regularly works a greater number of hours, days or shifts than are normally worked in a week by persons employed in full-time employment; and
-- src:328 | (b) the person is entitled to the period of leave under an employment agreement to compensate for the extra time worked.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 11(4) (src:326-328)
GIVEN `the week falls wholly or partly in a period of leave` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in each week the insured person regularly works a greater number of hours, days or shifts than are normally worked in a week by persons employed in full-time employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is entitled to the period of leave under an employment agreement to compensate for the extra time worked` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 11(4) the insured person is deemed to have worked a full working week` IF
        `the week falls wholly or partly in a period of leave`
    AND `in each week the insured person regularly works a greater number of hours, days or shifts than are normally worked in a week by persons employed in full-time employment`
    AND `the person is entitled to the period of leave under an employment agreement to compensate for the extra time worked`

-- src:317 | 11 (1) A week of unemployment for a claimant is a week in which the claimant does not work a full working week.
-- src:318 | Exception — no duties to perform
-- src:319 | (2) A week during which a claimant’s contract of service continues and in respect of which the claimant receives or will receive their usual remuneration for a full working week is not a week of unemployment, even though the claimant may be excused from performing their normal duties or does not have any duties to perform at that time.
-- src:320 | Exception — leave with deferred remuneration
-- src:321 | (3) A week or part of a week during a period of leave from employment is not a week of unemployment if the employee
-- src:322 | (a) takes the period of leave under an agreement with their employer;
-- src:323 | (b) continues to be an employee of the employer during the period; and
-- src:324 | (c) receives remuneration that was set aside during a period of work, regardless of when it is paid.
-- src:325 | Exception — compensatory leave
-- src:326 | (4) An insured person is deemed to have worked a full working week during each week that falls wholly or partly in a period of leave if
-- src:327 | (a) in each week the insured person regularly works a greater number of hours, days or shifts than are normally worked in a week by persons employed in full-time employment; and
-- src:328 | (b) the person is entitled to the period of leave under an employment agreement to compensate for the extra time worked.
-- A week of unemployment: the claimant does not work a full working week (subsection (1)), counting a week deemed to be
-- one (subsection (4)), and the week is not taken out by subsection (2) or (3).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 11 (src:317) (src:319) (src:321) (src:326)
GIVEN `the claimant works a full working week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insured person is deemed to have worked a full working week under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the week is not a week of unemployment under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the week or part of a week is not a week of unemployment under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 11 a week of unemployment for a claimant` IF
        `s 11(1) the week is a week in which the claimant does not work a full working week` (`the claimant works a full working week` OR `the insured person is deemed to have worked a full working week under subsection (4)`)
    AND NOT (`the week is not a week of unemployment under subsection (2)`)
    AND NOT (`the week or part of a week is not a week of unemployment under subsection (3)`)
